        <item>
            <title>0.16.0</title>
            <pubDate>Tue, 22 Sep 2026 12:20:28 +0700</pubDate>
            <sparkle:version>0.16.0</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>0.16.0</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>26.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <sparkle:hardwareRequirements>arm64</sparkle:hardwareRequirements>
            <description><![CDATA[<h2>What's new in 0.16.0</h2>
<ul>
<li>**The app is Rayto** — new name, new icon (a silver ribbon: an 8 on its way to ∞), a new intro. Your menus, shortcuts and settings carry over unchanged</li>
<li>**Opens like any Mac app** — Rayto is now signed and notarized by Apple: no &quot;damaged&quot; warning, no right-click → Open, no trip to Privacy &amp; Security to get it running</li>
<li>**Layers** — every menu can hold several layers of pills, one showing at a time. On an open menu press a layer&#x27;s key (1, 2, 3…) to switch — deeper layers come up from far away, going back is the same film in reverse. Make layers in Arrange: the row above the bar (&quot;1 2 3 +&quot;) — right-click a number to name it, pick its key, make it the layer the menu opens on, or delete it</li>
<li>**Setup, rebuilt** — one permission, then two short lessons (tap the key · hold it and swipe) on a practice menu that fires nothing real; trying a different key on the setup page is undone unless you press Continue</li>
<li>**File pills** — drop a file anywhere on the editor&#x27;s right side to use it; Change… opens in the folder the current file lives in</li>
<li>**The pill editor never grows** — the form scrolls, Add and Cancel stay where they are; the Add Pill search takes the arrow keys</li>
<li>**Corner dial** — the app under the dial no longer reacts to your pointer while you turn it</li>
<li>**Keyboard locked?** — when a password prompt has locked the keyboard (macOS Secure Input), the menu&#x27;s caption says so instead of ignoring your keys</li>
<li>**No Screen Recording request** — the app never asks for Screen Recording unless you turn on the iPhone display</li>
<li>**Sounds** — the default hover and navigation clicks now ship with the app (free, CC0 sounds)</li>
<li>**Feedback goes to hello@rayto.app** — the crash report and the feedback window write there; a false &quot;quit unexpectedly&quot; on a fresh install is fixed</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
